      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Revealing a specific, intentional, undocumented flaw—a \"signature secret\"—is a high-risk, high-reward strategy. If the flaw is genuinely unique and non-obvious, it functions as a definitive fingerprint that only the original author or someone privy to the initial design could immediately recognize. By demonstrating flawless knowledge of this buried detail, you force the narrative to pivot from style to impossible insider knowledge. While the corporate machine is massive, a genuine, unresolvable technical contradiction of their public story can sometimes cause enough internal chaos to force an acknowledgment.",
